WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Physical weathering breaks rock into pieces. Chemical weathering changes

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.520
minerals: feldspar can react to form clay and dissolved

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.440
products. These processes work together, but weathering is different

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.980
from carrying the products away. Transport abrades clasts and

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.140
sorts them. Watch rounded grains move with the current,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.240
then settle as flow weakens. Larger grains commonly settle

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.080
before smaller ones. Grain size, shape, and sorting record

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.080
different parts of this history. Burial pushes grains closer

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.140
together and reduces pore space. Minerals then precipitate between

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.020
grains and bind them. Compaction packs; cementation binds. Together

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.000
they contribute to lithification. Sedimentary rock forms here without

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.440
requiring the grains to melt.
